hadiths[17]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2125","Aishah narrated that she wanted to buy Barrirah but (her owners) stipulated that they should have her Wala'"
"2126","Abdullah bin 'Umar narrated that : the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited selling the Wala' and [from] conferring it. [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih. We do not know of it except as a narration of 'Abdullah bin Dinar from Ibn 'Umar from the Prophet (ﷺ). Shu'bah"
"2127","Ibrahim At-Taimi narrated from his father: ""'Ali delivered a Khutbah for us in which he said: 'Whoever claims that we have some book to read other than Allah's Book and this paper"
"2128","Abu Hurairah narrated : ""that a man from [Banu] Fazarah came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: 'O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)! My wife gave birth to black boy."" So the Prophet (s.a.w) said: ""[Do you have any camels?]"" He said: 'Yes."" He said: ""Then what are their colors?"" He said: ""Red."" He said: ""Is there a gray one among them?"" He said: ""Yes"
"2129","Aishah narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) visited her in a very happy mood, his face beaming with joy and said:\n\n  Don't you see that the Mujazziz looked just now at Zaid bin Harithah and Usamah bin Zaid, and said: 'These feet belong to each other.'  \n\n[Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih.\n\nSufyan bin 'Uyainah reported this Hadith from Az-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from 'Aishah and he added in it:\n\n  Dont you see that the Mujazziz passed by Zaid bin Harithah and Usamah bin Zaid while their heads were covered, and their feet were exposed, and he said: 'These feet belong to each other.'   This is how Sa'eed bin Abdur-Rahman - and more than one narrator - narrated this Hadith from Sufyan bin 'Uyanah, from Az-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from A'ishah. And this Hadith is Hasan Sahih. Some of the people of knowledge used this Hadith to support the case of Qa'if. \nJam e Tirmazi Hadees: 2129 Arabic Hadees: 2129"
"2130","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:""Give gifts"
"2131","Ibn 'Umar narrated that the Messenger of Allah (S.A.W)said:""The parable of the one who gives a gift"
"2132","Ibn 'Umar and Ibn 'Abbas narrated the Marfu Hadith:""It is not lawful for a man to give a gift and then take it back"
"2192","Mu'awiyah bin Qurrah narrated from his father that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""When the inhabitants of Ash-Sham become corrupt"
"2193","Ibn 'Abbas narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""Do not revert to disbelief after me"
"2194","Busr bin Sa'eed said:During the Fitnah(in the time) of 'Uthman bin 'Affan"
"2195","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""Rush to do good deeds. A Fitnah will occur that is like a portion of the dark night"
"2196","Umm Salamah narrated:""One night the Prophet (ﷺ) awoke and said"
"2197","Anas bin Malik narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""Before the Hour there shall be Fitan like a portion of the dark night. Morning will come upon a man as a believer"
"2198","Hisham narrated that Al-Hasan would say about the Hadith:"" Morning will come upon a man as a believer"
"2199","Alqamah bin Wa'il bin Hujr narrated from his father:""I heard the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) while a man was asking him: 'What do you see that we should do if there are leaders over us who deny our rights"
"2200","Abu Musa narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""Indeed after you there will be days in which knowledge shall be raised up and Al-Harj shall abound."" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah(s.a.w)! What is Al-Harj?"" He said: ""Killing"
